stands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Using Homonyms and Homophones"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Homonyms are made up of homophones and homographs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">homophone </span>is a word that has the same sound as another word but has a different meaning and may have a different spelling."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">right </span>and <span class=\"italic\">write </span><br/><span class=\"italic\">right </span>(noun) and <span class=\"italic\">right </span>(adjective)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">homograph </span>is a word that has the same spelling as another word but has a different sound and a different meaning."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">present </span>(noun) and <span class=\"italic\">present </span>(verb) <br/><span class=\"italic\">wind </span>(noun) and <span class=\"italic\">wind </span>(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "blue ... blew"}, {"type": "example", "content": "complement ... compliment"}, {"type": "example", "content": "pail ... pale"}, {"type": "example", "content": "won ... one"}, {"type": "example", "content": "know ... no"}, {"type": "example", "content": "pre<span class=\"strong\">sent</span> ... <span class=\"strong\">pre</span>sent"}, {"type": "example", "content": "excuse (s) ... excuse (z)"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing <span class=\"italic\">You</span> and <span class=\"italic\">I</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You stress <span class=\"italic\">you</span> and <span class=\"italic\">I</span> to add meaning and emphasis to a statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you stress a word, you make it longer, louder and a little higher tone. You can put stress on a word to emphasize it and make your meaning clearer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You stress <span class=\"italic\">you</span> or <span class=\"italic\">I</span> when you want to emphasize something about a person that is not expected."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I thought <span class=\"strong\">you</span> were going to find out.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>When you put stress on <span class=\"italic\">you</span>, you shift the emphasis to the other person.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read these sentences with stress on the bolded words.<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I thought <span class=\"strong\">you</span> were going to find out.</li><li>I thought <span class=\"strong\">you</span> were going to.</li><li><span class=\"strong\">I</span> was supposed to pay the bill while <span class=\"strong\">you</span> checked.</li><li><span class=\"strong\">You</span> might not care to go snorkeling but <span class=\"strong\">I</span> do.</li><li>No. <span class=\"strong\">I</span> definitely want to go snorkeling.</li></ul></span>"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le14ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to complement"}, {"type": "definiti